{"created": "2026-07-12T06:39:15.356693+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-12T06:39:15.518062+00:00", "id": 21318701, "conceptrecid": "21318700", "metadata": {"title": "Preliminary Summary of Distance-Exponent Readout by Independent Metric C and Relational Compensation Decomposition in an ABC Closed Phase System", "publication_date": "2026-07-12", "description": "This release publishes a preliminary summary of ABC closed phase system experiments designed to test whether adding an internal metric wave C can determine the distance exponent left open by the AB two-body experiments. The experiments introduce C-gauge validity windows, C-position controls, and decomposition of f_AB, f_AC, f_BC, and f_ABC. The results show acceleration-like AB relational compensation, but no native inverse-law or inverse-square-law dependence on position phase difference. Valid cases remained proportional-type, clarifying the boundary of the current one-dimensional localized-wave harmonic model.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kihara, Noriaki", "affiliation": "WF System Co., Ltd.", "orcid": "0009-0004-6753-4020"}], "keywords": ["ABC closed phase system", "independent metric C", "distance exponent", "relational compensation decomposition", "f_AB", "f_AC", "f_BC", "f_ABC", "inverse-square non-detection", "wave information readout"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21315735", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21308049", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21318696", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v1", "language": "eng", "license": "cc-by-4.0", "imprint_publisher": "Zenodo", "notes": "This paper does not deny inverse-square laws in general. It rejects only the narrower claim that the present one-dimensional AB harmonic mode